{
  "manufacturer": "ABB",
  "manufacturer_slug": "abb",
  "model": "ACS355 machinery drive (embedded Modbus RTU)",
  "model_slug": "acs355",
  "short_model": "ACS355",
  "aliases": [
    "ACS355-01E",
    "ACS355-03E",
    "ACS355-01U",
    "ACS355-03U",
    "ACS355 with FMBA-01"
  ],
  "equipment_type": "Variable frequency drive",
  "applies_to": "ACS355 drives with firmware 5.110 or later using the embedded fieldbus (Modbus RTU) over an FMBA-01 adapter on terminal X3 (EIA-485) or the panel port (RS-232).",
  "summary": "ABB's compact machinery variable frequency drive. Its embedded Modbus RTU slave is reached through the plug-in FMBA-01 RS-485 adapter (or point-to-point RS-232 on the panel connector) and maps the control word, two references, the status word and up to eight selectable actual values into 40001-40012, a 32-bit DCU-profile control/status pair into 40031-40034, and every drive parameter NNNN into register 4NNNN. This map covers the control block, group 01 operating data, fault and alarm words, fault history and the comm settings; all values are 16-bit.",
  "transport": [
    "RTU"
  ],
  "defaults": {
    "unit_id": 1,
    "baud": 9600,
    "parity": "None",
    "data_bits": 8,
    "stop_bits": 1,
    "tcp_port": null
  },
  "addressing": {
    "convention": "Modicon",
    "note": "The manual lists 4xxxx holding registers and states that register 4xxxx is sent as xxxx - 1 in the Modbus message (its example: 40002 is addressed as 0001), so 40001 = wire address 0. Drive parameter NNNN sits at register 4NNNN (e.g. 0103 -> 40103, wire 102; 3018 -> 43018, wire 3017). Registers that do not correspond to a parameter return an exception."
  },
  "default_word_order": null,
  "firmware": "ACS355 firmware 5.110 or later",
  "source": {
    "title": "ACS355 drives user's manual",
    "doc_number": "3AUA0000066143 Rev E",
    "revision_date": "2020-11-02",
    "url": "https://search.abb.com/library/Download.aspx?DocumentID=3AUA0000066143&LanguageCode=en&DocumentPartId=1&Action=Launch",
    "pages": "Embedded fieldbus chapter printed pp. 313-337 (setup pp. 315-318, reference scaling p. 322, function codes pp. 324-326, register mapping and 'xxxx - 1' rule pp. 325-326, exception codes p. 327, ABB Drives CW/SW pp. 329-332, DCU words pp. 333-337); FbEq definition pp. 179-180; groups 01/03/04 pp. 183-190; 1607 p. 213; 3018/3019 p. 255; group 53 pp. 290-292; 9802 p. 307; AC500 Modbus macro defaults p. 118"
  },
  "notes": [
    "There are no 32-bit registers: the manual states all values read or written are limited to 16 bits. Signals that can be negative (0101, 0105, 0106, 0110, 0111, 0112, 0404, 0405, 0408) are listed as INT16.",
    "Scaling is the manual's FbEq column (fieldbus integer per unit, e.g. '1 = 0.1 Hz' -> scale 0.1).",
    "40001 and 40004 work only with 5305 = ABB DRV LIM or ABB DRV FULL; 40031-40034 work only with 5305 = DCU PROFILE. ABB DRV LIM (the default) ignores control word bits 4 (RAMP_OUT_ZERO) and 10 (REMOTE_CMD).",
    "Actual values 40005-40012 follow 5310-5317 (defaults: 40005 = 0103, 40006 = 0104, 40007-40012 unassigned). Their scaling is that of the chosen signal, so they are left unscaled here; 40007-40012 are not listed.",
    "Reference scaling (ABB Drives profile): REF1 20000 = 1105 REF1 MAX (speed or frequency); REF2 10000 = 1108 REF2 MAX (speed, frequency, torque or PID). 1104/1107 minimums do not affect the scaling.",
    "Defaults conflict inside the manual: group 53 lists 5302 = 1, 5303 = 9.6 kbit/s, 5304 = 8 NONE 1 and 9802 = NOT SEL, while the AC500 Modbus macro sets station 2, 19.2 kbit/s, 5304 = 1 (which the parameter list calls 8 NONE 2), ABB DRV FULL and STD MODBUS. The text of that macro also mislabels 5302 as 5303. The macro also sets 3018 = FAULT and re-points 5310-5312 to 0101, 0303 and 0305, so 40005-40007 then read speed & dir, DCU status word LSW and fault word 1. Check the drive.",
    "0111 External ref 1 is in 0.1 Hz or 1 rpm depending on 9904 Motor ctrl mode, so it is left unscaled.",
    "Left out: 0120-0139 analog I/O, PID and process-variable signals (units depend on configuration), 0160/0414 DI status (panel and binary encodings differ), 0402/0403 fault time stamps, 0409 status at fault, and all motor/application parameters.",
    "The group 03 fault and alarm words are documented as read-only actual signals, but the alarm word text says an alarm can be reset by writing zero to the word; they are marked R here.",
    "5318 EFB PAR 18 is left out: the group 53 parameter list describes it as an extra response delay in ms, while the exception-code section says it holds the most recent exception code, so its meaning cannot be pinned down from the manual."
  ],
